      {
        "id": 118023,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-06T17:29:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think the ones of us that love him play him a lot.</p><p>We've had those awesome moments when things work out awesomely, and those are the great moments.</p><p>But we also enjoy the games where we are constantly struggling to get something done, because usually you end up playing a key part at some point in the match.</p><p>Fixer is not for you if you do not enjoy the struggling games, because he has a bunch of them. &nbsp;He is rarely dominant, most of the time useful in some way that isn't the way you'd like best, and sometimes he just struggles to do anything.</p><p>Every deck is different, and not everyone enjoys every hero. &nbsp;I personally don't enjoy Tempest, Ra, Chrono Ranger, Nightmist (non DW), Haka, Naturalist, The Sentinels, Scholar, Setback. &nbsp;I will play them, but I'd rather play someone else.</p><p>It isn't the players fault if they enjoy certain heroes more than others, I think we all understand that.</p><p>What frustrates me is when players complain that X Hero is terribly made or needs to be changed because they don't understand the deck or just don't like the playstyle. &nbsp;There are lots of heroes, we don't have to like them all.</p>",
        "post_number": 123,
        "post_type": 1,
