      {
        "id": 118024,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-06T17:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span>mutually agreed upon as useful and fun</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><span>Is it mutually agreed upon as being the only useful and fun combo? While I do think that Jack Handle is probably the most useful card going against Plague Rat, it is certainly not the only card I think Mr. Fixer has that would be useful. It is also certainly not the most fun option, infact due to the power Jack Handle has against Plague Rat, it probably slightly reduces my fun against Plague Rat since I will not be toying around with other things to try to win.</span></p>\n<p><span>Lets say I had an opening hand that consisted of Hoist Chain, Alternating Tiger Claw, and Overdrive against Plague Rat. I would be \"alright, got Hoist Chain, time to reduce his damage by 1, woo! If I am not infected and beating myself with the Hoist Chain next round, I will play Overdrive and reduce his damage by 2. If I am beating myself, I will instead play Alternating Tiger Claw and ignore the reduction to damage I have.\"&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span>Edited to repond to this:</span></p>\n<span>\n[quote=\"phantaskippy\"]\n<p>But we also enjoy the games where we are constantly struggling to get something done\n</p><p>\n[/quote]\n</p><p>I prefer using \"finding uses for what I have avaliable\".</p></span>",
        "post_number": 124,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:50:50.622Z",
