      {
        "id": 118026,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-06T18:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ronway:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Where did I say anything about only one fun combo against anything?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>We are discussing a particular combo in this thread, and acknowledging Fixer’s many other combos. Why could my hypothetical conversation not involve only a single combo for a particular situation? The subject was not “The myriad of combos Mister Fixer can execute.” It was “A single player’s positive experience with Mister Fixer using a particular combo in a single game.”</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>My issue was not with Fixer’s mechanics, or the execution of them. It was entirely about the meta of players discussing him, ignoring the frustrations presented by one side, then the other side talking over players’ heads if they didn’t respond with an affirmative, agreeable reaction about something fun they did not experience themselves.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Thank you, phantaskippy. I’ve found that to be the case with Fixer as well. Though he is not my favorite I enjoy DW Fixer’s playstyle quite a bit. I am happy that we could have a civil, straightforward, and respectable conversation about a character we have a differing perspective on.</p>",
        "post_number": 126,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:50:50.772Z",
