      {
        "id": 118030,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-08T19:38:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greywind\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/48/2006_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greywind:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Reckless, bad hands can happen to any of the heroes. Playing AZ on the app, his opening hand was all 4 of his Isothermic Transducer.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I understand that.&nbsp; What does my frustration have to do with bad hands?&nbsp; My frustration is with how people are interacting with one another.<br><br>An example from what you've just said:</p>\n<p>\"I love it when Zero has both of his Modules, Cold Snap, and Impale against Omnitron when he keeps recycling his Components in Insula Primalis.&nbsp; Your damage gets buffed and you can absorb a lot of fire damage to throw at him while you shred through Omni's field!\"</p>\n<p>\"I've not had that opportunity yet.&nbsp; It sounds like a lot of fun.&nbsp; Last game I played I got all four of his Isothermic Transducers in my opening hand.\"</p>\n<p>\"Well people really need to stop playing Zero's deck and start playing his hand!\"<br><br>No criticisms of deck mechanics or bad hands or individual characters.&nbsp; My frustration is squelching conversation by implying that another person's bad experiences are less relevant or outright invalid compared to one's own good ones.<br><br>This isn't a great injustice and I'm not gonna attach a \"-gate\" to anything to start some overblown campaign about it, but if I've seen anything come from these Fixer discussions it's that <strong>we aren't even having the same conversation</strong><strong> most of the time</strong>.&nbsp; I feel like if people focused on talking to each other rather than over one another then we'd have a much more productive discussion.</p>",
        "post_number": 130,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:50:51.047Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
