      {
        "id": 118031,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-08T20:56:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree with what Reckless is saying. A lot of times I find a hero less fun or more fun based on how one imposes their opinion/play experience of a certain character. For example, based on this thread I have a dichoctomy of opinions between becoming discouraged from playing Fixer due to his unusual mechanics, and also due to not being able to have a decent team contribution because he needs better resources.</p><p>On the other hand, I'm itching to have a few games with Fixer (as well as some of my lesser-played character choices) because I want to learn them better and deal with their best and worst hands, so I can better guage their potential and know what kind of plays to expect. To understand them better.</p>",
        "post_number": 131,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:50:51.131Z",
