      {
        "id": 118032,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-08T21:09:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would say I've had some great games with Mr. Fixer and some lackluster ones. &nbsp;A starting hand of overdrives and harmony is not much fun when the enemy has DR 1. &nbsp;And I'd say Mr. Fixer, and AZ are the most prone to have stalling hands at various points in the game. &nbsp;Those points are at the start and after board-wiping abilities. &nbsp; The next two heroes on the stall-out list for me are Fanatic and Expatriette. &nbsp;Each of these characters has some great cards and great combos but some cards are too particular or really work best with a combo. &nbsp;I think this is why those characters are less often chosen in games with people I know.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; Every character can get a stalling hand. &nbsp;I think these characters just have a higher chance of it.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
