        "created_at": "2014-12-08T21:11:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I agree with what Reckless is saying. A lot of times I find a hero less fun or more fun based on how one imposes their opinion/play experience of a certain character. For example, based on this thread I have a dichoctomy of opinions between becoming discouraged from playing Fixer due to his unusual mechanics, and also due to not being able to have a decent team contribution because he needs better resources.On the other hand, I'm itching to have a few games with Fixer (as well as some of my lesser-played character choices) because I want to learn them better and deal with their best and worst hands, so I can better guage their potential and know what kind of plays to expect. To understand them better.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is where Handelabra will help us. &nbsp;We can eventually play a ton of games with each of these heroes with only a medium expenditure of time, on solo games.</p>",
