        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-08T22:22:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>…And I'd say Mr. Fixer, and AZ are the most prone to have stalling hands at various points in the game. &nbsp;Those points are at the start and after board-wiping abilities. &nbsp; The next two heroes on the stall-out list for me are Fanatic and Expatriette. &nbsp;Each of these characters has some great cards and great combos but some cards are too particular or really work best with a combo.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'd put Unity way up there, too.&nbsp; I've seen lots of games where she either has no equipment, or no golems, for the first few rounds.</p>",
